  "content": [
   {
    "type": "heading_line",
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Last-minute pointers on those “what should you do/say next” questions"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 0,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": 0,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": null
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Generally speaking, whichever answer will keep the patient talking is a good answer"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 0,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": 0,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": null
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "In a patient hinting at suicidal thoughts, ALWAYS pick to ask them directly about suicidal ideation"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 0,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": 0,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": null
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "DO NOT challenge delusions"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "slide_card",
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "attrs": {
       "indLeft": 0,
       "indRight": 0,
       "indFirst": 0,
       "spaceBefore": 0,
       "spaceAfter": 0,
       "line": null,
       "align": "left",
       "shade": null,
       "borders": null,
       "marker": null
      },
      "content": [
       {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "If a patient states that they are acutely suicidal, the correct answer is generally to either send them to an ER or hospital for emergency evaluation/treatment"
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "attrs": {
       "indLeft": 0,
       "indRight": 0,
       "indFirst": 0,
       "spaceBefore": 0,
       "spaceAfter": 0,
       "line": null,
       "align": "left",
       "shade": null,
       "borders": null,
       "marker": {
        "text": "•",
        "font": null,
        "marks": [],
        "tabPt": 12
       }
      },
      "content": [
       {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "If you are in the ED doing the evaluation, correct answer is to hospitalize the patient"
       }
      ]
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 0,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": 0,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": null
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "In a verbally agitated patient, verbal de-escalation techniques (asking how you can help, acknowledging their frustration) is generally correct"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 0,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": 0,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": null
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "In a physically aggressive patient, emergency IM haloperidol/lorazepam/diphenhydramine is generally the correct answer"
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
